---
description: Security requirements for the 7Oz Espresso Cafe platform.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Security

Assume every request is malicious.

Validate everything.

Trust nothing.

---

# Authentication

JWT Access Token (Bearer)

Refresh Token Rotation

Refresh token stored in HTTP-only Secure Cookie

Password hashing

Argon2id

Strong password policy.

---

# Authorization

RBAC only.

Never trust frontend roles.

Always validate permissions server-side.

MVP roles:

Customer

Admin

Super Admin

---

# Secrets

Never hardcode:

Passwords

API Keys

JWT Secret

SMTP Credentials

Database URL

Use environment variables.

---

# Validation

Validate:

Body

Params

Query

Headers

Uploads

---

# SQL Injection

Use parameterized SQL via sqlc / pgx.

Never concatenate SQL strings.

---

# XSS

Escape output.

Sanitize rich text.

Never store refresh or access tokens in localStorage.

---

# CSRF

Refresh tokens use HTTP-only cookies.

Therefore:

Enable CSRF defenses for cookie-authenticated refresh flows.

Validate Origin / Referer.

Use SameSite cookie attributes.

Access tokens sent via Authorization Bearer do not replace cookie CSRF controls for refresh.

---

# File Upload

Validate:

Extension

Mime Type

File Size

Filename

Virus scanning should be future-ready.

---

# Rate Limiting

Apply to:

Login

Register

Forgot Password

OTP

Reservation submission (including guest bookings)

Contact form

---

# Logging

Never log:

Passwords

Tokens

Secrets

Payment information

---

# HTTPS

Production always requires HTTPS.

Never allow insecure production deployment.

---

# Dependencies

Use maintained libraries.

Remove abandoned packages.

Run dependency audits regularly.

---

# Goal

Security is a default,

not an optional feature.
